# CMS content edits

When the user asks to change live CMS copy (blogs, news, FAQs, careers, terms, writers, or QA Guide body text), use `scripts/cms-content.mjs`. Do not add a SQL migration for a content edit, and do not tell the user to paste it into the admin UI unless the script cannot reach the CMS.

## Blogs — Lovable blogs-api

Blog reads and writes do **not** use `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. That key is not in `.env.local`. Do not search for it, and do not report that blog edits failed because it is missing.

`scripts/cms-content.mjs` sends blog commands to the Lovable Cloud function `https://<project>.supabase.co/functions/v1/blogs-api`. Auth comes from `.env.local`:

- `BLOGS_API_KEY` as the `x-api-key` header
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` as `apikey` and `Authorization: Bearer`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` for the function host

`PATCH` must include `slug` in the JSON body. The same commands as below work; the script routes `blogs` itself. News is not on this function.

The script writes only with `--apply`. Run a dry run first, then apply. Other tables still need `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` when that key exists.

```bash
node scripts/cms-content.mjs list blogs --q "keyword"
node scripts/cms-content.mjs get blogs --slug the-slug --full
node scripts/cms-content.mjs update blogs --slug the-slug --set seo_title="New title"
node scripts/cms-content.mjs update blogs --slug the-slug --patch ./patch.json --apply
```

- Tables: `blogs`, `news_updates`, `faqs`, `qa_guides`, `terms_content`, `job_openings`, `job_organizations`, `writers`.
- FAQs, terms, organizations, and writers match on `--id`, not `--slug`.
- Long body copy: `--set content=@./body.md` or a JSON `--patch` file.
- QA Guide publish tier, robots, and URL changes stay on `PATCH /api/posts/:id`. This script edits guide copy only.
- Database updates fire the existing revalidate webhook, so production pages refresh without a deploy.

Case study pages at `/case-studies` render `src/lib/case-studies-data.ts`. Edit that file for copy visitors see. The `case_studies` table is not what those pages read.
